## Lore

Reaver Raiders are criminals given a license. They are robbers and
cutthroats with real skill at theft, hold-ups and armed raids, most of them
good in the saddle or on a motorcycle or hover vehicle, and a Warlord keeps
them for exactly that.

They work in bands, from a dozen highwaymen up to a platoon and now and then
a whole company turned loose on a fortified town. The job is to strip the
enemy, D-Bees, foreigners and rival War Camps of supplies and valuables, to
bleed an opponent by taking his resources and picking off his people, and
sometimes simply to punish a community that has displeased the Warlord.

A raid is noise on purpose: whooping riders, wild gunfire, fires, dragged
smoke and explosions, all of it to spread panic and make the band look
bigger than it is while a quieter group goes for the real prize. Encircling
a victim and posting snipers in trees or on rooftops are favorite tricks.

Nobody in the War Camp likes them. They are seen as bullies and thieves,
and the Cossacks and War-Knights despise them outright. The same training
also describes an independent bandit or highwayman with no Warlord at all.

## GM Notes

Printed as "O.C.C. & NPC Villain"; it is a playable class, and the same
stats serve for bandits, highwaymen and raiding bands with no tie to the
Warlords. A player bandit known to have ridden with a notorious gang is
probably a wanted criminal with a price on his head: expect combat and hot
pursuit from War Camps, communities, Hero-Knights and other authorities, and
Huntsmen, bounty hunters, mercenaries, adventurers and outlaws after the
reward, justice or revenge. Most villagers will not deal with a bandit
except under duress.

Trick Shooting: the Raider picks any one of the six abilities under the
skill. +2D6 S.D.C. is rolled once at creation. The save vs Horror Factor
rises by +1 at levels 2, 4, 6, 8, 10 and 12.

Related skills at level one: two must come from Rogue or Espionage, and four
more are free choices.

Starting kit beyond what the sheet lists: one weapon for each W.P. with
1D4+1 extra clips apiece, a folding shovel, a bedroll, belt, boots and a
handful of personal items. The armor is homemade (30-60 M.D.C.) or any
modern suit of 30-100 M.D.C. available in the region.

Vehicle: a partial bionic horse with barding, or a battered hovercycle,
motorcycle or similar small vehicle suited to fast raids and escapes. It
looks shabby and is missing 1D4x10 M.D.C. from its main body, but is
otherwise in good condition.

Money is 1D6x100 credits plus 1D6x100 credits of tradeable goods. Salary is
500 credits a month with food, basic clothing and equipment and medical
attention, plus a 10% cut of the spoils of raids the Raider takes part in,
and sometimes bonus items or another 5-10% for an especially good job.

No cybernetics to start; about half pick up a bionic limb and/or a handful
of implants. Secret resources: none to start, but ties to fences, smugglers
and Gypsies are likely, and some risk the Black Market despite the
Warlords'' disapproval. Special weapons, explosives, equipment, vehicles and
troops may be issued by assignment.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'reaver-bandit-raider');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
